          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "The pattern is best indexed by an **orthorhombic** cell. The apparently tetragonal sequence at 15.83\u00b0, 17.50\u00b0, 21.80\u00b0, and 27.56\u00b0 is the \\(010/011/012/013\\) series. A consistent indexing is:\n\n- \\(a \\approx 7.5305\\) \u00c5\n- \\(b \\approx 5.5946\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c \\approx 11.8890\\) \u00c5\n- \\(V \\approx 500.9\\) \u00c5\u00b3\n- \\(Z=4\\), calculated density \\(\\approx 4.81\\) g cm\\(^{-3}\\)\n\nThe absence of \\(h0l\\) reflections with odd \\(h\\), together with observed odd \\(00l\\) and \\(0k0\\) reflections, favors **Pma2, No. 28**. Representative indexing includes 001 at 7.43\u00b0, 002 at 14.89\u00b0, 010 at 15.83\u00b0, 011 at 17.50\u00b0, 012 at 21.80\u00b0, 003 at 22.42\u00b0, 200 at 23.61\u00b0, 201 at 24.78\u00b0, 013 at 27.56\u00b0, and 202 at 28.02\u00b0.\n\nThe lattice and space group are considerably more secure than the Li/F coordinates; the latter should be treated as a chemically constrained starting model for Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_KBaLiZnF6\n_audit_creation_method\n'Powder-indexed Pma2 starting model; light-atom coordinates require refinement'\n\n_chemical_name_common                 'potassium barium lithium zinc fluoride'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'K Ba Li Zn F6'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'KBaLiZnF6'\n_chemical_formula_weight              362.74\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 4\n\n_cell_length_a                        7.5305\n_cell_length_b                        5.5946\n_cell_length_c                        11.8890\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          500.89\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn         4.81\n\n_space_group_crystal_system           orthorhombic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P m a 2'\n_space_group_IT_number                28\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x,y,z'\n3  'x+1/2,-y,z'\n4  '-x+1/2,-y,z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nK1   K    4 d  0.246  0.165  0.074  1.0  1.20\nBa1  Ba   4 d  0.248  0.642  0.565  1.0  0.75\nLi1  Li   4 d  0.026  0.176  0.359  1.0  1.30\nZn1  Zn   4 d  0.018  0.679  0.858  1.0  0.70\nF1   F    4 d  0.032  0.185  0.191  1.0  1.00\nF2   F    4 d  0.036  0.670  0.026  1.0  1.00\nF3   F    4 d  0.247  0.423  0.303  1.0  1.00\nF4   F    4 d  0.249  0.900  0.772  1.0  1.00\nF5   F    4 d  0.474  0.171  0.515  1.0  1.00\nF6   F    4 d  0.470  0.660  0.687  1.0  1.00\n```\n\nA centrosymmetric model with the same metric is a possible powder-only alternative, but it does not account as naturally for the observed extinction pattern and ordered K/Ba\u2013Li/Zn chemistry.",
